# Backend

Use NestJS.

Use Repository Pattern.

Use Service Layer.

Use DTO.

Use Validation Pipe.

Use Guards.

Use Interceptors.

Use Exception Filters.

Never access database directly inside controller.

Business logic belongs inside services.

Structure features under `src/features/<feature>/` with module, controller, service, repository, dto, and types.

Controllers handle HTTP only — parse input, call service, return response.

Repositories encapsulate all Prisma/database access.

Use class-validator and class-transformer for DTO validation.

Use `@nestjs/config` for environment configuration — never hardcode secrets.

Return consistent error shapes via exception filters.
